            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GRAMSON"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is sooo good! I, too, only added 1/2 c sugar. I never use half and half so I decided to use evaporated milk instead. I didn't want to waste the other 8 oz of evap milk so I just poured the 12 oz can into a 4 c measure and then filled with milk and heated it all. I didn't bother with adding some cold milk to the hot chocolate. Yum Yum, just what I wanted on a cool morning, thanks Jeanie Bean!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Aida E"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I’ve been trying to replicate the hot chocolate in Italy which was thick and super delicious. While this wasn’t as thick, the flavor was excellent. For 2 servings I included 2T Klim powdered milk with cocoa, sugar, salt and water mix + 2% milk &amp; vanilla, cooked as directed. I served and topped it with whipped cream.",
            "datePublished": "2020-02-15T17:39:38.613Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rachael Hunter Smith"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent hot cocoa!!! As mentioned in other reviews it was quite sweet and each serving only makes enough for a small styrofoam cup size. I just used my regular mug, made the chocolate mixture with hot water from the tap, filled to the top with milk (to cut down on sweetness and make a full serving), and microwaved until hot. Super easy and no extra pans to wash!",
            "datePublished": "2020-02-28T16:30:17.770Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nicole Dias"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was delicious! I followed the advice in cutting the sugar to 1/3c (I’m diabetic and I don’t like overly sweetened drinks) and added 1/2c of strongly brewed coffee to deepen that chocolate flavor. I altered the milk to cream ratio slightly for a creamier hot chocolate. The sweetness was perfect. The creaminess was perfect. The chocolate was perfect. I used Ghirardelli powdered chocolate as my preferred chocolate source (and in my opinion is the BEST chocolate to use in any recipe calling for chocolate).",
            "datePublished": "2021-12-22T23:55:38.243Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sunshlne"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wowza! This is amazing hot cocoa! I imagine this is how Judy’s cocoa from The Santa Clause tastes. Like someone else described, it tastes like a melted chocolate bar! I followed the directions except for reducing the sugar to 1/2 cup as recommended in reviews. I also used homemade vanilla paste. I’d say if you use quality cocoa and vanilla and reduce the sugar (start low and add to taste) you’re going to love this decadent hot cocoa!",
            "datePublished": "2022-12-03T22:25:50.910Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Elyazoid"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good! Nice and rich,. personally I didn’t use the cream, because it tasted as though it didn’t need it. (Note: only use 1/2 cup sugar. 3/4 is overwhelming)",
            "datePublished": "2020-11-18T15:35:24.260Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jennie C"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Too sweet, but otherwise fine. I used 1/2 cup sugar and I like that better. Also increased the salt to about 1/8 tsp.",
            "datePublished": "2020-03-15T23:08:14.077Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mary"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I doubled the recipe and made this one cold winter night for guests in our home. I made the cocoa-sugar mix ahead of time then slowly mixed it in the milk when the guests arrived. I cut the sugar in half, as per many reviews, and prepared sweetened whipped cream for the topping. WONDERFUL!!!",
            "datePublished": "2021-12-20T23:27:19.783Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jayme M"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I thought this recipe was the one I made two years ago, but I could’ve sworn the one I made called for heavy cream, and incorporated it into the hot cocoa-not called for it to be added to the mugs separately. So, I added the heavy cream to the mugs, but it made the hot cocoa too cool. Next time I’ll put the cream in the hot cocoa itself, and reduce the sugar to 1/2, as others suggested. Also, I added a little Bailey’s. Yum!",
            "datePublished": "2022-12-11T01:17:26.899Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Susan Fischer Mathews"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Used 1/2 cup monk fruit instead of sugar. Mixed the milk and cream in at the same time. Almost like drinking chocolate, delicious, rich and decadent!",
            "datePublished": "2023-01-30T23:02:00.712Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Faye B"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious. Quick and easy on the stove top, but I have to confess: It didn't serve four -- it served one, because I made it while I was alone and drank all of it. I've made it three or four times since I found this recipe. I halved the recipe a couple of times, since the full recipe takes nearly a quart of half-and-half.\nI made it with a little less sugar and a little more cocoa since I like a stronger chocolate taste. I also used half-and-half instead of simply whole milk.",
            "datePublished": "2019-12-26T01:33:51.317Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "kitkatagogo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Used 1/2 C sugar and it was still a bit too sweet for my tastes. Easily modified. Other than that, I thought it was perfect!",
